hooks.prompt:
Act as a read-only pre-commit cleanliness gate. Read .claude/skills/pre-commit-cleanup/SKILL.md and use its criteria. Inspect git status, the unstaged diff (git diff), and the staged diff (git diff --cached). Do not edit files.

If the pending changes are clean (no AI running notes, temporary plans, prompt fragments, debugging artifacts, redundant comments, or excessive documentation), return exactly:
{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "allow", "permissionDecisionReason": "Diff is clean."}}

If cleanup is needed, return exactly:
{"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "deny", "permissionDecisionReason": "<list each file and specific issue found>"}}

Then instruct the main Claude session to invoke /pre-commit-cleanup before retrying the commit. Hook input: $ARGUMENTS
